MERE.RUN EXPANDED CORE ML CONVERSION (2026-10-13)
------------------------------------------------
The optional expanded bundle adapts export/eg2_text.py and export/eg2_audio.py
from the pinned EverPaper revision. Text attention uses fused Core ML SDPA
with query scaling that preserves the original unit attention scale; local
attention remains bidirectional through distance 512. The host supplies token
embeddings. Long text and the 30-second audio encoder use float32 computation.
Text functions cover 1024, 2048, 4096, and 8192 positions; audio consumes native
log-mel features and frame, half-frame, and token masks. The short-input
FluidInference graphs and their original weights remain unchanged.
The original Google checkpoint is revision
914f7f89142e33e77833254d9c9b90c3cef7303b (Apache-2.0).

MERE.RUN PACKED CORE ML INFERENCE (2026-10-13)
-------------------------------------------
PackedEmbeddings.swift adapts the token-isolated packing and bounded concurrent
prediction approach in FluidInference/FluidUse's EmbeddingGemma2Manager.swift,
revision d278e17df85e39e8c21bb64a467da81c39576fcd, licensed under Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidUse/tree/d278e17df85e39e8c21bb64a467da81c39576fcd
The Apache-2.0 license text is retained in LICENSE. The upstream license has no
project-specific copyright notice beyond the standard license appendix.
Modifications: actor-owned lazy loading, persistent compilation caching,
order-preserving batching, individual long GPU predictions, and caller-owned
sessions integrated with mere.run's ordered multimodal contract.
This section describes additional mere.run adaptations; the earlier EverPaper
notice describes the original EverPaper distribution.
